    test(gitreins): bound the tier-2 criteria so the judge can grade them (QA-CRIER-064)
    
    The four tier-2 runs that starved UNEXAMINED for crier all exhausted the
    600-iteration rung with "0 of 1 criteria graded", and none of them ever ran a
    gate command. Their recorded tool calls page an unbounded evidence set one line
    per call:
    
      06fb79f8 QA-CRIER-58  600.4 iters /  5.3M in  140 distinct `grep -o ... | sed -n 701p`, 702p, ...
      a503d646 QA-CRIER-60  600.9 iters / 22.0M in  the same command re-issued 166 times verbatim
      0f0e80e1 QA-CRIER-57  600.7 iters / 38.5M in  `git show <sha>:<file> | sed -n '532,542p'` then 533,543 ...
      92778507 QA-CRIER-57  600.2 iters / 38.1M in  `git show <sha> -- <file> | sed -n '476p'`, 477p, ...
    
    The rungs above them have been raised four times (iterations 100->250->400->600,
    input 9M->12M->16M->24M->48M) and the identical "0 of 1 graded" signature came
    back after each, so a fifth raise buys more scrolling, not a verdict. The starved
    resource is the CRITERION's missing proof obligation: each of the four criteria
    was created thin (no PROOF:/FAILIF:) and in wave-cell vocabulary that resolves
    nowhere in the tree, so the judge had to invent its evidence set and could never
    name its end.
    
    - .gitreins/CRITERIA.md (new): the authoring rules -- carry PROOF:/FAILIF:,
      resolve every noun against the tree, never write an enumeration as a search
      obligation, keep the gate inside the judge's 30s command cap or cite a
      committed evidence file, split what fails independently -- plus the measured
      diagnosis table and the re-judge procedure.
    - .gitreins/config.yaml: criteria.enforce: refuse (GR-172) so a thin criterion
      can no longer be created; a comment block in the evaluator section records
      that the iteration/token rungs are NOT to be raised for an UNEXAMINED run and
      why (measured basis, run ids).
    - .gitreins/tasks.yaml: the QA-CRIER-58 and QA-CRIER-60 criteria are rewritten
      as bounded compound criteria with file:line anchors -- the same claims, with
      "chaos-resource legs" resolved to the real package command, "all three
      failures" resolved to the two named test entry points, a PROOF command that
      runs in ~4s (inside the tool cap), and a committed evidence file for the leg
      this host cannot inject.
    
    explicitly NOT done: no cap raise (the one-raise rule does not apply to a run
    that never reached its criterion -- see the config comment), and no tool-side
    change (gitreins 0.21.0's 30s run_command cap is DF-CRIER-506; its UNEXAMINED
    outcome still has no distinct pass_class, so the "UNGRADED as a pass_class" arm
    of the acceptance criteria remains tool-side).
    
    Re-judge proof lands in the following commit (two sequential tier-2 runs on this
    branch, examined=true read from .gitreins/history/<date>/<run>/verdict.json).
    
    Addresses QA-CRIER-064.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
