+# GR-172 criterion authoring gate (QA-CRIER-064, 2026-11-17): `refuse` makes
+# `gitreins task create` REJECT a criterion that carries neither `FAILIF:` nor a
+# command/locator-shaped `PROOF:` (engine/criteria.py::criterion_gaps; the tool's
+# own default policy is `warn`, which only prints). The four rows that starved
+# tier-2 (QA-CRIER-57 runs 0f0e80e1 + 92778507, QA-CRIER-58 run 06fb79f8,
+# QA-CRIER-60 run a503d646) were all created thin: the criterion named no proof,
+# so the judge had to invent the evidence set and paged it one line per tool call
+# (140 distinct `sed -n Np` commands in 06fb79f8; the same command 166x in
+# a503d646) until the iteration cap ended the run with 0 of 1 criteria graded.
+# Authoring rules + the measured diagnosis: .gitreins/CRITERIA.md. A wave that
+# genuinely needs a thin row must pass --allow-thin and say why in its brief.
+criteria:
+  enforce: refuse
