+  # ── NO FURTHER RAISE FOR UNEXAMINED RUNS (QA-CRIER-064, tick 2026-11-17) ──
+  # The rungs above have been raised four times (iterations 100→250→400→600,
+  # input 9M→12M→16M→24M→48M) and the UNEXAMINED signature came back at every
+  # one of them. The four starved runs measured for this row all ended with
+  # "0 of 1 criteria graded":
+  #   0f0e80e1 QA-CRIER-57  600.7 iters / 38.5M in / 0 of 1 graded
+  #   92778507 QA-CRIER-57  600.2 iters / 38.1M in / 0 of 1 graded
+  #   06fb79f8 QA-CRIER-58  600.4 iters /  5.3M in / 0 of 1 graded
+  #   a503d646 QA-CRIER-60  600.9 iters / 22.0M in / 0 of 1 graded
+  # None of them ran a single gate command: their recorded tool calls page an
+  # unbounded evidence set one line per call (06fb79f8: 140 distinct
+  # `grep … | sed -n Np`; a503d646: one command re-issued 166x). Raising a cap
+  # buys more of the same scrolling — the starved resource is the CRITERION's
+  # missing proof obligation, not the budget. Fix the criterion
+  # (.gitreins/CRITERIA.md, enforced by `criteria.enforce: refuse` above); only
+  # raise a rung when a run that has a COMPLETE, BOUNDED evidence set starves,
+  # and cite its usage.jsonl numbers as the rungs above do.
 
